{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlMarkovTraceInstance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlMarkovTraceInstance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.MarkovTraceInstance","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlMarkovLevelR","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlNormalisation"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.wtraceW_ne_of_level_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.wtraceW_ne_of_level_ne","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L337-L348","doc":"**Distinct levels give distinct traces** — the contrapositive, stated as the inequality it is,\nand needing only `q ≠ 0` and `q² ≠ 1`.\n\nThe two traces already differ at the *single* element `σ₀ ∈ H_1(q)`.  So the level is not merely\ndetermined by the whole functional: one evaluation separates every pair of levels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.eq_wenzlWtrace_of_markov_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.eq_wenzlWtrace_of_markov_real","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L327-L335","doc":"**Uniqueness at every level, over `ℝ`, with no genericity hypothesis.**\n\n`eq_wenzlWtrace_of_markov` with `hgen` discharged by `realGen_of_sq_ne_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.realGen_of_sq_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.realGen_of_sq_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L307-L325","doc":"**`hgen` over `ℝ`** — the `ℝ` case of `gen_of_notRootOfUnity`, kept under its old name.\n\nOver `ℝ`, `NotRootOfUnity q` is itself equivalent to `q ≠ 0 ∧ q² ≠ 1` (a real root of unity is\n`±1`), so the hypothesis carried through the level-`r` chain adds\n**nothing** over `ℝ` beyond `q² ≠ 1`.\n\nThis is worth stating because the scope notes on the level-`r` files read as though genericity were\na live restriction — \"at a root of unity `H_n(q)` is not semisimple and partitions stop indexing the\nirreducibles\".  That is true of the *general* theory, and it is exactly why the hypothesis is there;\nbut over the real base ring the excluded locus is `{q² = 1}` and nothing else.  In particular it does\n**not** exclude the substrate value: `q₀ ≈ 1.10998` has `q₀² ≈ 1.232 ≠ 1`, so the level-`r` Markov\ntrace exists there for every `r ≥ 1`.\n\nReading this the other way is the caution: it does not say the general-`Q` statements are stronger\nthan they look.  Over `ℂ`, or over a cyclotomic field, `hgen` is a real hypothesis and the level-`r`\nweight genuinely fails without it.  What is vacuous is the *specialisation to `ℝ`*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.gen_of_notRootOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.gen_of_notRootOfUnity","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L296-L303","doc":"**`hgen` follows from `NotRootOfUnity q`, over any field**: `(q²)^k = q^{2k}` and `2k ≠ 0`.\n\nSo every `hgen` in the level-`r` chain is implied by the `hq2` it is carried beside. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.level_unique_of_wenzlMarkovTrace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.level_unique_of_wenzlMarkovTrace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L273-L292","doc":"**Distinct levels give distinct traces.**\n\nIf the level-`r` and level-`s` weighted seminormal traces agree on every `H_n(q)` — indeed, if they\nagree at the single element `σ₀ ∈ H_1(q)` — then `r = s`.\n\nThis is the composition the two uniqueness statements admit: `param_eq` reads the parameter off the\ntrace, and `level_unique_of_markovParameter` reads the level off the parameter.  Neither alone says\nthis.  In particular the level is not extra bookkeeping attached to the trace; it is **recoverable\nfrom one value of it**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wenzlMarkovTrace_two_tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wenzlMarkovTrace_two_tr","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L258-L267","doc":"**Conservativity: at `r = 2` the level-`r` trace is `wtrace`**, the convention-D object of\n`MarkovTraceInstance` — pointwise, on every `H_n(q)`.  A generalisation that does not contain its\nown special case is a different object wearing the same name; this is the evidence that this one\ndoes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.eq_wenzlWtrace_of_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.eq_wenzlWtrace_of_markov","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L243-L256","doc":"**Uniqueness of the Markov trace at every integer level `r`.**\n\n*Every* Markov trace on the Hecke tower whose parameter is the level-`r` Wenzl parameter is the\n`wenzlWeight r (q²)`-weighted seminormal trace.  At `r = 2` this is\n`MarkovTraceInstance.eq_wtrace_of_markov` (see `wenzlMarkovTrace_two_tr`).\n\nThe uniqueness argument is `markovTrace_unique`, unchanged and level-free; what makes the statement\navailable at level `r` is `wenzlMarkovTrace`, the instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wenzlMarkovTrace_tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wenzlMarkovTrace_tr","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L239-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wenzlMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wenzlMarkovTrace","kind":"def","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L223-L237","doc":"**The level-`r` Markov trace.**\n\n`w = wenzlWeight r (q²)` at `z_r = Q^r / (q · [r]_Q)`, `Q = q²`.  The three weight inputs are\nexactly the three theorems #5662 generalised: `sum_dim_wenzlWeight_eq_one`,\n`sum_addable_wenzlWeight_all`, `markov_wenzlWeight`.  Nothing else is needed, and in particular no\nlevel-specific argument appears — the level enters only through those three. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.markovTraceOfWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.markovTraceOfWeight","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L201-L219","doc":"**Any weight with normalisation, branching and the Markov condition is a Markov trace.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_markov","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L184-L199","doc":"The Markov condition, in the `genMat` form the corner assembly produces, gives the\n`MarkovTraceFamily` Markov axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_incl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_incl","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L135-L182","doc":"**Branching of the weight gives consistency under the inclusion.**\n\nThe representation-theoretic half — corner decomposition of the diagonal sum,\n`compress_seminormalRep_heckeIncl`, the corner↔addable reindexing — is weight-agnostic; the weight\nenters only in the last line, as `hbranch`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_one","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L120-L133","doc":"Normalisation of the weight gives `tr(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L111-L118","doc":"**Cyclicity needs no property of `w` at all** — `seminormalRep` is an `AlgHom`, so this is\n`Matrix.trace_mul_comm` blockwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW_apply","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L106-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.wtraceW","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovTraceInstance.lean#L90-L104","doc":"The seminormal trace weighted by an arbitrary `w`.\n\n`wtrace` is the `w = ocneanuWeight q z_D` case; the level-`r` trace below is the\n`w = wenzlWeight r (q²)` case.  Keeping `w` free isolates exactly which of the four\n`MarkovTraceFamily` axioms depend on the weight (three) and which does not (cyclicity). ","signatureChunk":0}]}